# p5 mcp: the config writer's oracle (MCP-C, E1 + A7). fx v0.0.16's `/mcp add`
# and `/mcp remove` edit `~/.fx/mcp.json` and the workspace's `.mcp.json` in
# place; `home` and `workls` keep the bytes they leave. The profile is the old
# `{"mcp":…}` shape with keys, numbers and escapes fx doesn't know (the
# migration case); the workspace file is 4-space JSON with a key of its own.
# The stdio server is p5-mcp-stdio.ts, which both files name by `@BUN@` and
# `@SCENARIOS@` (capture.sh writes both in). xfx is given the same files; its
# `/mcp` verbs are MCP-V's, so its side of these bytes is the writer's unit
# test (`src/mcp/config.rs`) until they land.
# `web` is mcphttp in `hang`: `connecting` through `list`, 10 s after its add,
# where a refused port ended its first try's 10 s probe right then.
mcphttp hang
work p5-mcp-config-ws
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-config-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-config-profile.json
wait 5
home before
workls before
type /mcp add two -- @BUN@ @SCENARIOS@/p5-mcp-stdio.ts
key Enter
wait 3
type /mcp add --env K=v --env Z=1 three -- @BUN@ @SCENARIOS@/p5-mcp-stdio.ts --flag
key Enter
wait 3
type /mcp add --header X-Team=core web http://127.0.0.1:@MCPPORT@/web
key Enter
wait 3
type /mcp add --project p2 -- @BUN@ @SCENARIOS@/p5-mcp-stdio.ts
key Enter
wait 3
snapfull added
home after-add
workls after-add
type /mcp list
key Enter
wait 4
snap list
key Escape
wait 0.3
key C-u
type /mcp remove --project p2
key Enter
wait 3
type /mcp remove old
key Enter
wait 3
type /mcp remove three
key Enter
wait 3
type /mcp remove web
key Enter
wait 3
snapfull removed
home end
workls end
